From cbfbdd2fd68726000a53f04505d1a9b5e33c67c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 00:16:48 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 48/50] v4.8-gpu: correct the stats note and GPU comments

Three text corrections:

  - The divergence stats note said 'tasks flagged' but the sustained
    divergence flag now counts one episode per 3+ consecutive divergent
    sleeps (INFINITY_DIVERGENCE_STREAK), not one per sleep.  The note
    reads 'sustained episodes' to match the counter semantics.

  - The idle-compensation blend comment claimed the mul_u64_u32_div
    result 'is exact for any value'; each term is truncated, so the
    result is at most 1 ns below the exact convex combination.  The
    comment now says the blend cannot overflow and quantifies the
    truncation error as far below vtime ordering precision.

  - The pass-over walk comment claimed per-selection cost O(K) instead
    of O(N); the walk itself can still traverse ineligible nodes beyond
    K, only the credited accounting (and its locked atomics) is bounded.
    The comment now states that distinction precisely.

Signed-off-by: Galih Tama <galpt@v.recipes>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c | 12 ++++++++----
 kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c          |  2 +-
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c
index 46c9233fc..16af2af5c 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/scheduler/sched_main.c
@@ -191,8 +191,10 @@ static inline u64 drm_sched_entity_calc_vtime(struct drm_sched_entity *entity)
 			 * plain multiply wraps u64 once min_gpu_vtime >=
 			 * 2^48 ns (~3.26 days of accumulated GPU time).
 			 * mul_u64_u32_div computes the products in 128-bit
-			 * intermediates, so the blend is exact for any
-			 * value.
+			 * intermediates, so the blend cannot overflow; each
+			 * truncated term keeps the result at most 1 ns below
+			 * the exact convex combination, far below vtime
+			 * ordering precision.
 			 */
 			effective_total =
 				mul_u64_u32_div(rq->min_gpu_vtime,
@@ -476,8 +478,10 @@ drm_sched_rq_select_entity_infinity(struct drm_gpu_scheduler *sched,
 		 * nearest entities are the closest to the next pick (most
 		 * relevant for starvation feedback); entities deeper than K
 		 * are credited on subsequent selections as the winner moves.
-		 * This keeps per-selection cost O(K) under rq->lock instead
-		 * of O(N) for clients with many contexts.
+		 * This bounds the credited work (and the locked atomics) to K
+		 * entities per selection; the walk may still pass over
+		 * ineligible nodes beyond K, but the expensive per-entity
+		 * accounting is bounded.
 		 */
 		if (entity->infinity_pid) {
 			struct rb_node *rb2;
diff --git a/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c b/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
index a7d39843f..b9eca42fc 100644
--- a/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched/infinity_sched.c
@@ -329,7 +329,7 @@ static int infinity_stats_proc_handler(const struct ctl_table *ctl, int write,
 
 	cpu_rows[9].label = "EMA vs PELT divergence";
 	fill_pretty_llu(cpu_rows[9].value, sizeof(cpu_rows[9].value), dvg);
-	strscpy(cpu_rows[9].note, "tasks flagged", sizeof(cpu_rows[9].note));
+	strscpy(cpu_rows[9].note, "sustained episodes", sizeof(cpu_rows[9].note));
 
 	/* ---- RT rows ---- */
 	rt_rows[0].label = "RT throttles";
